{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.104,
            0.372,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "INTRODUCTION TO TRIGONOMETRY"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.863,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "119"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.159,
            0.155,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": "Then"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.422,
            0.146,
            0.538,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{ AC }{ AB } = \\frac{ PR }{ PQ }",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.214,
            0.205,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.199,
            0.898,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{AC}{PR} = \\frac{AB}{PQ} = k,\\  say\\tag{1}",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.247,
            0.412,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": "Now, using Pythagoras theorem,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.271,
            0.628,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{BC} = \\sqrt{\\mathrm{AB}^2 - \\mathrm{AC}^2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.314,
            0.142,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "and"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.309,
            0.629,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{QR} = \\sqrt{\\mathrm{PQ}^2 - \\mathrm{PR}^2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.349,
            0.77,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "BC √AB2 -AC² √k2PQ2−k2PR2 k√PQ2-PR2 So, QR √PQ2- PR2 √PQ2-PR2 √PQ2-PR2 = k"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.868,
            0.373,
            0.898,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "(2)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.41,
            0.357,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "From (1) and (2), we have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.422,
            0.436,
            0.604,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{AC}}{\\mathrm{PR}} = \\frac{\\overline{\\mathrm{AB}}}{\\mathrm{PQ}} = \\frac{\\overline{\\mathrm{BC}}}{\\overline{\\mathrm{QR}}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.488,
            0.802,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "Then, by using Theorem 6.4, $\\Delta \\mathrm{ACB} \\sim \\Delta \\mathrm{PRQ}$ and therefore, $\\angle \\mathbf { B } = \\angle \\mathbf { Q }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.523,
            0.595,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": "Example 3 : Consider $\\Delta   \\mathrm { A C B }$ right-angled at C, in which $\\mathrm { A B } = 2 9$ units, BC = 21 units and $\\angle ABC = \\theta$ (see Fig. 8.10). Determine the values of"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.594,
            0.3,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "(i) $\\cos ^ { 2 } \\theta + \\sin ^ { 2 } \\theta ,$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.622,
            0.301,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $\\cos ^ { 2 } \\theta - \\sin ^ { 2 } \\theta$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.643,
            0.514,
            0.898,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_6_image_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.649,
            0.399,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": "Solution : In $\\Delta   \\mathrm { A C B }$ , we have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.679,
            0.612,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{AC} = \\sqrt[3]{\\mathrm{AB}^{2} - \\mathrm{BC}^{2}} = \\sqrt{(29)^{2} - (21)^{2}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.722,
            0.694,
            0.82,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 8.10"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.284,
            0.722,
            0.804,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": "\\ln { \\sqrt { ( 2 9 - 2 1 ) ( 2 9 + 2 1 ) } } = { \\sqrt { ( 8 ) ( 5 0 ) } } = { \\sqrt { 4 0 0 } }   = 2 0   { \\mathrm { u n i t s } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.771,
            0.136,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.757,
            0.538,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": "\\sin \\theta = \\frac{AC}{AB} = \\frac{20}{29}, \\cos \\theta = \\frac{BC}{AB} = \\frac{21}{29}.",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_24.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.805,
            0.774,
            0.851
          ],
          "content": "Now, (i) $\\cos ^{2}\\theta +\\sin ^{2}\\theta =\\left ( \\frac{20}{29} \\right ) ^{2} +\\left ( \\frac{21}{29} \\right ) ^{2} =\\frac{20^{2} +21^{2}}{29^{2}} =\\frac{400+441}{841} =1,$"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.857,
            0.769,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": "and (ii) $\\cos ^{2}\\theta -\\sin ^{2}\\theta =\\left ( \\frac{21}{29} \\right ) ^{2} -\\left ( \\frac{20}{29} \\right ) ^{2} =\\frac{(21+20)(21-20)}{29^{2}} =\\frac{41}{841}$"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
